course: dictionary
lesson: 15337
title: Words that rise high
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «The eagle was soaring over the valley, its wings wide and still.» The eagle is not flapping. It is floating high in the air, so soaring means flying high and gliding.
explain: «Prices are soaring this year, so the bread costs more every week.» Prices are not birds, so soaring must mean something else here. The prices are going up very quickly. Ask yourself: what is going up fast?
explain: Soaring can also describe something very tall, like «soaring towers», or a strong feeling, like «her spirits were soaring». The context tells you which meaning fits, so always read the words around it.
fact: Soaring is the -ing form of soar. Soar, soars and soared come from the same word.
fact: «Soaring» means flying high in the air, often gliding without flapping wings.
fact: «Soaring» can mean going up very quickly, like prices or temperatures.
fact: «Soaring» can also mean very tall or rising high, like «soaring mountains».
fact: «Soaring» can describe strong, rising feelings: «her spirits were soaring» means she felt very happy and hopeful.
exercise: «The eagle was soaring over the valley.» What is the eagle doing? | Sleeping in a nest | Running on the ground | Swimming in a lake | *Flying high, gliding without flapping
exercise: «Prices are soaring, so the bread costs more every week.» What does soaring mean here? | Staying exactly the same | *Going up very quickly | Hiding under the table | Falling slowly to the ground
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means rising high in the air: «The kite was soaring above the park.» | *soaring | the | kite | park
test: «Her spirits were soaring after the good news.» What does soaring show about her? | She was lost in the dark | *She was very happy and hopeful | She was tired and sleepy | She was cold and wet
test: «The soaring towers could be seen for miles.» What does soaring mean in this sentence? | Going up in price | Very quiet and still | *Very tall and rising high | Full of water
exam: «Temperatures are soaring this week, so the children are going to the pool.» Why does the author choose soaring? | To show the temperature is falling | To show the children cannot swim | *To show the temperature is going up very fast | To show the pool is closed
